  "notes": "ダサい is a slang i-adjective meaning unfashionable, uncool, or lame.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nOrigins disputed. Possibly from ⟦{田舎|いなか}→田舎：01320_inaka⟧ (countryside) + さい, implying 'country bumpkin style.'\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverbial: ダサく\n- Te-form: ダサくて\n- Past: ダサかった\n\nUSAGE:\nCan describe fashion, behavior, ideas, or people. Usually written in katakana. Common in casual speech, especially among younger speakers.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦かっこ{悪|わる}い→かっこわるい：10759_kakkowarui⟧: uncool (more neutral)\n- {格好|かっこう}{悪|わる}い: unfashionable (formal)\n- イケてない: not cool (slang)\n\nOpposite: ⟦かっこいい→かっこいい：09378_kakkoii⟧ (cool, stylish).",
